Package: thunderbolt-frame-dkms
Version: @VERSION@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms (>= 2.1.0.0), kmod, make, libc6, thunderbolt-tbfix-dkms (= @VERSION@)
Recommends: usb4-rdma-provider (>= 0.2.72), linux-modules-extra-generic-hwe-24.04-edge | linux-modules-extra-generic-hwe-24.04 | linux-modules-extra-generic
Conflicts: thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms, thunderbolt-tbrxe-dkms
Replaces: thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms, thunderbolt-tbrxe-dkms
Maintainer: AppMana <ops@appmana.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/AppMana/forks-thunderbolt
Description: thunderbolt_frame + thunderbolt_frame_rxe RDMA engine (DKMS source)
 DKMS source package for thunderbolt_frame.ko (session + lossless frame
 service on Thunderbolt XDomain rings) and thunderbolt_frame_rxe.ko
 (rxe-derived InfiniBand engine over the frame service). Both modules build
 in one DKMS pass: thunderbolt_frame links against the thunderbolt-tbfix
 core's Module.symvers and generated header shim, thunderbolt_frame_rxe
 links against thunderbolt_frame's Module.symvers, so this package is
 version-locked to the exact thunderbolt-tbfix-dkms release (never mix
 revisions).
 .
 The modules are NOT autoloaded: no modules-load.d entry is installed.
 Loading is a deliberate act: `modprobe thunderbolt_frame_rxe` (depmod pulls
 in thunderbolt_frame). A node runs one RDMA engine at a time; this package
 conflicts with and replaces the previous thunderbolt-tbrxe-dkms (the same
 modules under their old tbframe/tbrxe names) and the retired
 thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms, and userspace needs usb4-rdma-provider >= 0.2.70
 to bind the engine's driver id.
